{# Shared <head> contents for all layouts. #}
{%- set metaDescription = description if description else "Ralph Hawkins is a service designer working in the public sector with NHS England, helping people stay healthy." -%}
{%- if not description and content -%}{%- set metaDescription = content | excerpt -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- set pageTitle = title if title else "Ralph Hawkins" -%}
{%- set ogType = "article" if (tags and 'weeknotes' in tags) else "website" -%}
{#- Explicit image front matter wins; otherwise week notes and the homepage
    get a generated card (see src/_11ty/og-images.js). -#}
{%- set ogImage = image -%}
{%- if not ogImage and tags and 'weeknotes' in tags -%}{%- set ogImage = '/images/og/' + page.fileSlug + '.png' -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if not ogImage and page.url == '/' -%}{%- set ogImage = '/images/og/home.png' -%}{%- endif -%}
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<!-- Preload fonts -->
<link rel="preload" href="/fonts/volksans/volksans-Normal.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" href="/fonts/volksans/volksans-SemiBold.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" href="/fonts/volksans/volksans-Bold.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/images/favicon.png">
{%- if tags and 'weeknotes' in tags %}
{#- Post pages get an SVG favicon in the post's seeded blob colours; the PNG
    above stays as the fallback for browsers without SVG favicon support. #}
<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="{{ page.fileSlug | blobFavicon }}">
{%- endif %}
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
{#- The phone's browser chrome, carrying the post's colour at the same 20%
    mix --color-overscroll takes on <html> in base.njk. One value for the
    gutter above and below the page and the bar around them.

    It is a diluted colour and not the foot (postColor) on purpose: this is a
    large flat area abutting the page, not a mark identifying the post.

    **It is a tint now, not a match, and that is worth knowing before it is
    changed.** There was no theme-color between 2026-08-11 and 2026-08-30; it
    came back because Ralph asked for it once main flooded the post with the
    blob's own colour and the bar had something to match. It was driven per
    frame from random-gradients.js then, because a static hex cannot follow a
    fill that ramps in over half a viewport and a hue that turns 40deg per
    viewport scrolled. The fill came off on 2026-09-03 and the script's copy of
    it went too: the body of a post away from the disc is the plain background
    again, so there is no flat ground left for the bar to track — only a soft
    radial that the tracking deliberately never modelled.

    So this is now a static per-post tint sitting above a page that is not
    quite that colour. Kept rather than removed, because Ralph asked for a
    coloured chrome and the gutter carries the same value; the alternatives are
    the bare background, or dropping the meta again as it was before
    2026-08-30. Weeknotes only, gated like data-blob-hue — the listing pages
    and the 404 have no post colour to carry, and a hue rolled at random is not
    a thing to paint a browser with.

    iOS caches this aggressively, so a stale tint in an already-open tab is not
    evidence of a bug. #}
{%- if tags and 'weeknotes' in tags %}
<meta name="theme-color" content="{{ page.fileSlug | blobOverscroll }}">
{%- endif %}
<meta name="description" content="{{ metaDescription }}">
<link rel="canonical" href="{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}">
{#- Feed autodiscovery: how a reader finds the week notes from any page. #}
<link rel="alternate" type="application/atom+xml" title="Ralph Hawkins – week notes" href="{{ site.url }}/feed.xml">

<!-- Open Graph / Twitter -->
<meta property="og:type" content="{{ ogType }}">
<meta property="og:site_name" content="Ralph Hawkins">
<meta property="og:locale" content="en_GB">
<meta property="og:title" content="{{ pageTitle }}">
<meta property="og:description" content="{{ metaDescription }}">
<meta property="og:url" content="{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}">
{%- if ogImage %}
<meta property="og:image" content="{{ site.url }}{{ ogImage }}">
<meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
<meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
<meta property="og:image:alt" content="{{ pageTitle }}">
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
{%- else %}
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary">
{%- endif %}
<meta name="twitter:title" content="{{ pageTitle }}">
<meta name="twitter:description" content="{{ metaDescription }}">
{%- if ogImage %}
<meta name="twitter:image" content="{{ site.url }}{{ ogImage }}">
{%- endif %}

<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/main.css">
<title>{% if title %}{{ title }} – {% endif %}Ralph Hawkins</title>

{# Structured data, defined once for every layout. Week notes describe a
   BlogPosting; every other page describes the site as a whole. #}
{% if tags and 'weeknotes' in tags %}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BlogPosting",
  {#- dump JSON-encodes the value (quotes included) and safe skips HTML
     autoescaping — inside a script block entities like &quot; would be
     read as literal text, not decoded. #}
  "headline": {{ title | dump | safe }},
  "datePublished": "{{ date | isoDate }}",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Ralph Hawkins",
    "url": "{{ site.url }}"
  },
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Ralph Hawkins"
  },
  "mainEntityOfPage": {
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "@id": "{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}"
  }
}
</script>
{% else %}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebSite",
  "name": "Ralph Hawkins",
  "url": "{{ site.url }}",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Ralph Hawkins",
    "jobTitle": "Service Designer",
    "worksFor": {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": "NHS England"
    }
  }
}
</script>
{% endif %}

<script src="/js/random-gradients.js"></script>
